    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1069">

                <pb facs="0934" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4107b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sparks</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-08T19:00:00-05:00">November 8, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Chargé’s personal letter to Duggan<anchor n="53" xml:id="d1069-f1"/> and
                    Department’s telegram 177, November 1, 5 p.m. Department understands that the
                    request of the Haitian Government will be for a temporary reduction for the
                    period of this fiscal year.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
